      "Compromised base image beaconing to a command server"
    ],
    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": {
      "cause": "Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228): logging the User-Agent made Log4j resolve ${jndi:ldap://…}.",
      "why": "log4j-core before 2.15.0 performs lookups on logged messages, so a JNDI string in any logged header makes the JVM call the attacker's LDAP server, which can point it at remote code. Isolate the host, treat it as compromised, upgrade log4j-core (2.17.1+), and restrict egress.",
      "tell": "Under 100 ms after the UA is logged, the app host itself opens TCP to the exact host:port in the payload, then a second port. A probe that only gets logged makes no callback."
    },
    "source": {
      "title": "Apache Log4j Security Vulnerabilities (CVE-2021-44228)",
      "url": "https://logging.apache.org/security.html"
    }
